id: breaker
name: Breaker
kind: crafting
slots: 1
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Apparel hit with it loses twice the Break Value; a Weapon hit with it takes a quarter (rounded
  up) more Damage.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: its Effects line as printed, word for
# word, cut into one line to an effect, each opening with its tag as the rulebook writes one.
summary: >
  [Passive]: If you hit a piece of Apparel with this Weapon, double the loss of Break Value. If
  you hit a Weapon instead, increase the Damage dealt to that Weapon by 1/4 (rounded up).
text: >
  Breaker: This Weapon is designed to deal extra damage to inanimate objects.
  –Weapon Type: All
  –Prerequisites: N/A
  –Quality Slots: 1
  –Effects: If you hit a piece of Apparel with this Weapon, double the loss of Break Value. If
  you hit a Weapon instead, increase the Damage dealt to that Weapon by 1/4 (rounded up).

---

# The Break Value it takes off the Top Layer is 2 where it would be 1 - off a Called Shot at the
# Apparel, and off a Health Threshold, by the table's ruling. A Weapon it hits - a Called Shot at
# one, or a Shield Blocking it - takes 1/4 of the blow more, before that Weapon's own Damage
# Reduction.
[passive]
weapon.breaker = true;
